  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1216 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nHot and rain-free weather continues through the week with the \nsubtropical ridge staying near the area. Temperatures are forecast \nto steadily rise as the airmass warms, with highs entering the 100-\n105 range in more widespread fashion by late week. Heat indices may \nclimb more into the 105-110 range especially at lower elevations mid \nto late week. This could necessitate issuance of heat related \nproducts. \n\nHot and dry conditions may continue into Saturday, but a shift in \nthe weather pattern ushered by the ridging moving farther favors a \nchange in conditions over South Central Texas this weekend. As the \neastern periphery of the ridge lines up with the Plains, northerly \nflow will be favored aloft. This may bring a weak front or trough \ninto our area this weekend, accompanied by rain chances and a \npotential cooldown to below average temperatures towards the start \nof August if the front remains intact.",
